{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('../submission.schema.json'))['\"'$defs'\"']\nfor k in ['ClaimDraft','Grounding','BindingDraft']:\n print(k,json.dumps(s.get(k),indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"ClaimDraft {\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\": {\n      \"title\": \"Id\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"kind\": {\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"obligation\",\n        \"assumption\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"Kind\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"concern\": {\n      \"default\": \"implementation_semantics\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"consensus_safety\",\n        \"bounded_liveness\",\n        \"implementation_semantics\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"Concern\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"description\": {\n      \"title\": \"Description\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"source_ids\": {\n      \"description\": \"Located materials; file kinds do not establish normative authority\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Source Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"scope\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Scope\"\n    },\n    \"pending\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Pending\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"grounding\": {\n      \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Grounding\",\n      \"default\": {\n        \"source_ids\": [],\n        \"expectation_ids\": [],\n        \"binding_ids\": [],\n        \"derivation\": \"\",\n        \"applicability\": \"\",\n        \"unresolved\": [],\n        \"conflicts\": [],\n        \"alternatives\": []\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"id\",\n    \"kind\",\n    \"description\",\n    \"source_ids\",\n    \"scope\",\n    \"pending\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"ClaimDraft\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\nGrounding {\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"source_ids\": {\n      \"description\": \"Exact IDs of acquired implementation source materials; not Behavior or Binding IDs\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Source Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"expectation_ids\": {\n      \"description\": \"Exact IDs of acquired materials supporting the expectation; not invented expectation labels. Explain normative applicability in derivation.\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Expectation Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"binding_ids\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Binding Ids\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"derivation\": {\n      \"default\": \"\",\n      \"title\": \"Derivation\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"applicability\": {\n      \"default\": \"\",\n      \"title\": \"Applicability\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"unresolved\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Unresolved\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"conflicts\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Conflicts\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"alternatives\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Alternatives\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"title\": \"Grounding\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\nBindingDraft {\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"associations\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/BindingAssociation\"\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Associations\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"anchor\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CodeAnchor\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null\n    },\n    \"id\": {\n      \"title\": \"Id\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"material_id\": {\n      \"title\": \"Material Id\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"symbol\": {\n      \"description\": \"Source symbol tied to a verified declaration, interface member or explicitly declared call-site anchor. The behavior range may be a narrow internal snippet. Do not substitute arbitrary words from the excerpt.\",\n      \"title\": \"Symbol\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"start_line\": {\n      \"title\": \"Start Line\",\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"end_line\": {\n      \"title\": \"End Line\",\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"description\": {\n      \"title\": \"Description\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"pending\": {\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Pending\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"associations\",\n    \"id\",\n    \"material_id\",\n    \"symbol\",\n    \"start_line\",\n    \"end_line\",\n    \"description\",\n    \"pending\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"BindingDraft\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"VerifyLeader is documented as a way to prevent stale FSM reads after leadership loss. Its threshold counts voters, but it registers callbacks on all replication peers. The next discriminator is a single partition history: let the voter majority elect a new leader and complete a command, then call VerifyLeader on the former leader while it can still contact a nonvoter. That can distinguish an API failure from callback arithmetic alone.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > select_verify.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v3.json'))\nfor a in m['activities']:a.pop('behavior_ids',None)\nfor f in m['facts']:\n for k in ['established_by','consumed_by']:f.pop(k,None)\nm['version']=3\nm['behaviors'].append(dict(id='B-verify-notify',primary_activity='A2',execution_owner='Per-peer followerReplication.notifyAll',protocol_context='Pending verifyFuture pointers registered on one replication worker',trigger='Heartbeat or replication invokes notifyAll with a boolean result',implementation_guards=['notifyLock serializes extraction and replacement of pending notify map'],reads=['Pending notify map and supplied leader boolean'],writes=['Replace notify map before calling each future.vote(leader)'],external_effects=['Invoke vote on each captured verification future'],produces_fact_ids=['F-verify-callback'],source_ids=['S-notify','S-heartbeat','S-match','S-snapshot-send'],unknowns=['Boolean argument contains no explicit voter identity or suffrage; legal successful producer history still requires execution.']))\nm['facts'].append(dict(id='F-verify-callback',meaning='A replication worker drained a particular verifyFuture from its pending notification map and invoked that future vote callback with the worker result boolean. A true boolean is not itself a claim of voter eligibility.',identity={'verification':'verifyFuture pointer','producer':'followerReplication object and peer ID at registration','generation':'captured leader replication generation'},validity_context='Future was registered and remained in that worker map until notifyAll; callback may arrive before or after other peers notify',representation=['verifyFuture.vote(leader) invocation'],durability='Volatile callback; no durable authority record',recovery='Pending verification is failed/cleared on leader exit, not reconstructed',source_ids=['S-notify','S-verify-start','S-verify-count','S-leader'],unknowns=['Same-history relationship between callback producer, voter eligibility, later election and public result has not been executed.']))\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id']=='B-verify':\n  b['consumes_fact_ids']=['F-verify-callback']\n  b['source_ids']+=['S-verify-api','S-suffrage']\n  b['unknowns']=['Can nonvoter callbacks yield public VerifyLeader success after a different voter-majority leader has completed a command in the same history? Independent lease, negative callbacks and ordinary replication may instead stop the former leader.']\nchanges={'B-verify':dict(impact='dependency',source_ids=['S-notify','S-verify-start','S-verify-count','S-verify-consume','S-verify-api','S-suffrage'],rationale='Name the actual callback assertion consumed by existing verification aggregation; preserve voter-threshold and all-peer registration observations.',preserves='No accepted Candidate or Unit exists. Existing commitment and generation facts are unchanged; callback delivery is kept distinct from eligible authority support.')}\nsources=[dict(id='S-verify-api',file='api.go',start_line=880,end_line=895,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='S-suffrage',file='configuration.go',start_line=8,end_line=24,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='S-verify-tests',file='raft_test.go',start_line=1866,end_line=1973,kind='test_expectation'),dict(id='S-inmem-init',file='inmem_transport.go',start_line=37,end_line=110,kind='code_observation')]\nq=dict(question='After a voter majority has elected a different leader and that leader has completed an Apply in the same partition history, can the former leader return nil from a subsequently invoked VerifyLeader by consuming callbacks from a connected nonvoter?',importance='The public VerifyLeader contract supports preventing stale FSM reads after leadership loss. A false successful result could allow callers to trust a former leader. This question measures authority-confirmation semantics; it does not assert divergent committed logs or an observed application read.',source_ids=['S-verify-api','S-suffrage','S-verify-start','S-verify-count','S-verify-consume','S-notify','S-heartbeat','S-peers','S-lease','S-verify-tests'],participants=['Former leader A','Voter majority B and C','Nonvoter D'],objects=['verifyFuture','Per-peer notification map','Configuration','Public Apply future'],contexts=['Stable configuration with three voters and one nonvoter','A partition retaining A-D contact and B-C majority contact','Verification invocation after B or C has completed Apply'],event_paths=['Bootstrap and actual elections/configuration changes establish configuration','Partition voter links to A while preserving A-D and B-C links','B or C becomes leader and completes a uniquely identified Apply','Invoke VerifyLeader on A; correlate its own completion and worker callbacks'],activity_classes=['A2'],behavior_ids=['B-verify-notify','B-verify'],fact_ids=['F-verify-callback'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-heartbeat':'Real peer RPCs produce verification notification booleans','B-election':'The separate majority must acquire authority through actual campaign workers','B-config-change':'Public configuration operations establish voter/nonvoter roles','B-lease':'Independent loss-of-contact protection may end A authority before observation','B-generation':'Leader exit fails pending verification; cannot omit this protection','B-consume':'Majority Apply completion supplies observed post-election progress'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Lease check counts only voters and can step down the former leader.','Negative verification notification, higher-term ordinary replication response or incoming RPC may terminate old authority.','Existing verification tests cover all-voter success, partial connectivity and failure after forced higher term; they do not establish this mixed-suffrage history.','Nonvoter exclusion is explicit for election/commitment, while the VerifyLeader API states a public stale-read purpose rather than a detailed callback algorithm.'],unknowns=['Applicable requirement: confirm that successful post-majority-progress VerifyLeader is incompatible with the public current-leader contract; do not infer voter-only callback rules solely from code.','Initial prefix and producer: construct actual election, stable membership and peer acknowledgments without assigning critical protocol state.','Same history/faults: transport partition must prevent stale voter replies from satisfying the target verification while retaining all protective workers.','Endpoint: correlate one VerifyLeader completion after the new leader Apply completion; no stale application read has been observed.'],priority=3,trigger_rationale='The code computes a voter-only threshold but registers each verification future on every replication worker, including nonvoters. notifyAll passes only a boolean to a counter. A post-new-leader public completion comparison tests the user-visible meaning while keeping callback eligibility as a cause hypothesis.',preferred_check='controlled_schedule',disposition='needs_specific_evidence')\njson.dump(m,open('map-verify.json','w'),indent=2)\nsub=dict(action='continue',map_path='map-verify.json',map_changes=changes,sources=sources,question=q,rationale='Select public authority verification over pipeline call-order and split persistence leads: the observed all-peer callback registration has a direct public stale-read consequence and a feasible actual-worker partition discriminator. Save the callback lifecycle now; next construct an exploratory same-history harness before deriving the precise obligation. Preserve the usable overview and independent frontier leads.')\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-verify.json','w'),indent=2)\nimport jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(m,json.load(open('../product-schemas.json'))['ConsensusAuditSpec'])\njsonschema.validate(sub,json.load(open('../submission.schema.json')))\nfor x in sources:assert x['end_line']<=len((Path('../agent-source')/x['file']).read_text().splitlines())\nprint('Products and citation bounds checked locally.')\nPY\npython3 select_verify.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
